# Project Rules: bike-mechanic-pad

## 1. Core Vision & Ethos
- Purpose: A 100% local-first, offline-first digital clipboard for solo bike mechanics.
- License: GPLv3 (Copyleft - must remain free, open-source, and user-owned).
- Target UX: Designed for dirty hands at the repair stand. High contrast dark mode, large touch targets, keyboard-driven navigation (hotkeys like Ctrl+K or /), and zero layout bloat.

## 2. Technical Architecture (Phase 1 MVP)
- Execution: Single-device local execution only.
- Tech Stack: SvelteKit + Tailwind CSS + Embedded Local SQLite (SQLite Wasm / OPFS for browser storage, or Tauri for desktop).
- Storage Layer: Direct reads/writes to local SQLite.
- Backups: Manual local database export/download (.db file).
- Offline Persistence: Ensure the app works seamlessly offline with zero network connection after initial page load (via Service Worker / PWA manifest or Tauri runtime).

## 3. Strict Guardrails & Anti-Patterns
- NO backend servers, APIs, or REST microservices.
- NO cloud databases (Postgres, Prisma, Supabase, Firebase).
- NO user accounts, logins, session tokens, or OAuth integrations.
- NO multi-device delta sync or cloud folder watchers in Phase 1.
- DO NOT suggest cloud hosting infrastructure or paywalled backend tools unless explicitly asked.

## 4. Code Standards & Patterns
- Keep components modular, self-contained, and lightweight.
- Use explicit foreign keys, indexing, and clean relational SQLite schemas.
- Prioritize sub-5ms local UI rendering and database queries.